From bd27e00c01a950d6052b97172ed08833e44eb35c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 14:47:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add hot-leads dashboard, stuck-lead alerts, richer rubric

Three follow-on features on top of the qualification watchdog:

- Dashboard: GET /hot serves an HTML table of qualified leads sorted by
  ai_qual_score (or ?format=json), so managers call the warmest first.
  Guarded by ORDERS_API_KEY (header or ?key=). db.getHotLeads backs it;
  renderHotHtml is a pure, HTML-escaped (XSS-safe) renderer.
- Stuck-lead alerts: the watchdog now flags hot leads (score >= 60) where
  the client wrote last and no manager reply for > N hours (defaults via
  WATCHDOG_STUCK_HOURS / WATCHDOG_STUCK_MIN_SCORE) and sends a digest
  alert. isStuck() is pure/tested; findStuckLeads scans chats via the new
  db.getLastMessage.
- Richer rubric: qualify.js gains explicit 0-100 score bands in the
  system prompt and two new profile fields (category, next_step). The
  dashboard falls back to niche/summary for leads scored under the old
  schema, so nothing breaks; a `qualify.js --restale` run refreshes them.

9 new tests (32 total pass).
